-- title:
--   Small-extension lifting step for the Lubin–Tate universal law
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a complete discrete valuation domain $W_0$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, together with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative one-dimensional formal group law over $k$ satisfying `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. (with the ideal taken to be $\bot$) its $q$-th series is a unit multiple of the Drinfeld divisor $\mathrm{drinfeldDivisor}\ q\ 0\ 0$, and let $F_u$ be a commutative formal group law over $\mathrm{PowerSeries}\ W_0$ whose coefficientwise image under $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ is $F_0$. Assume the universality hypothesis `hFu1`: for every Artinian local $W_0$-algebra $T$ with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_T$ onto $k$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, whose maximal ideal squares to zero and in which $q = 0$, and every commutative formal group law $G$ over $T$ that is the base change of $F_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_T$, there is exactly one $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : \mathrm{PowerSeries}\ W_0 \to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \varphi = \mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ for which some base change $G'$ of $F_u$ along $\varphi$ admits an isomorphism of laws $\psi : G' \to G$ (a power series with zero constant term, unit linear coefficient, intertwining the two laws) whose coefficients reduce to those of $X$, that is $\mathrm{res}_T(\mathrm{coeff}_n \psi) = \delta_{n,1}$. Now let $T$ and $S$ be Artinian local $W_0$-algebras with such residue maps $\mathrm{res}_T$ (compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$) and $\mathrm{res}_S$, and let $\sigma : T \to S$ be a surjective $W_0$-algebra map with $\mathrm{res}_S \circ \sigma = \mathrm{res}_T$ and $\ker \sigma \cdot \mathfrak{m}_T = 0$ (a small extension). Let $G$ be a commutative formal group law over $T$ that is the base change of $F_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_T$, let $G_\sigma$ over $S$ be the base change of $G$ along $\sigma$, and suppose given a $W_0$-algebra map $\bar\varphi : \mathrm{PowerSeries}\ W_0 \to S$ with $\mathrm{res}_S \circ \bar\varphi = \mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$, a base change $\bar G'$ of $F_u$ along $\bar\varphi$, and an isomorphism of laws $\bar\psi : \bar G' \to G_\sigma$ whose coefficients satisfy $\mathrm{res}_S(\mathrm{coeff}_n \bar\psi) = \delta_{n,1}$. Then there is exactly one $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : \mathrm{PowerSeries}\ W_0 \to T$ with $\sigma \circ \varphi = \bar\varphi$ for which some base change $G'$ of $F_u$ along $\varphi$ admits an isomorphism of laws $\psi : G' \to G$ with $\mathrm{res}_T(\mathrm{coeff}_n \psi) = \delta_{n,1}$ for all $n$.
--
--   This is the small-extension step in the Lubin–Tate analysis of the deformation functor of a one-dimensional formal group law of height two over $k$: deformations over $T$ rigidified as above lift uniquely along a small surjection $T \to S$ once a rigidified lift over $S$ is given. In this edition the universality input `hFu1` is required only over test algebras killed by $q$, which is what the induction uses; the result feeds the passage from square-zero universality to universality over all Artinian local test algebras ([`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.universal_of_universal_sq_zero`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.universal_of_universal_sq_zero)).
